#heading(level: 1, numbering: none, outlined: true)[ABSTRACT]

Web application testing at the Department of Information Technology, Politeknik Negeri Malang, faces challenges in ensuring the quality of academic applications such as Kompen, Jayanti, and Whistleblower. Conventional server-uptime monitoring cannot guarantee that an application's core functions -- login, role-based access control (RBAC), input validation, and CRUD operations -- actually work correctly, while automation testing tools such as Selenium, Cypress, and Playwright still require manual test case authoring, which becomes a bottleneck. TathyaTest is presented as an automatic test case generator that crawls the rendered DOM using Playwright, builds an element model and a per-role access matrix, and then generates and executes functional test cases automatically. This research measures the effectiveness of TathyaTest in generating automatic test cases, improving functional test coverage, and validating application functional expectations. The Prototyping method is applied iteratively from a simple CRUD prototype to Playwright integration for cross-browser testing (Chrome, Firefox, WebKit), evaluated on three case-study subjects (a Laravel Blade application, a Laravel Inertia-React application, and SauceDemo as an external baseline).

Evaluation results show 100.0% element-model coverage on all three subjects, 87.5% route coverage on both Laravel subjects, and a 100.0% mutation score (9 of 9 seeded faults detected) with 100.0% fault-localization accuracy and perfect cross-browser agreement (Fleiss' kappa κ = 1.00). TathyaTest generated 103 test cases per Laravel subject and 31 test cases for SauceDemo, with an estimated 29--31× time saving compared to manual test authoring (Mann-Whitney U, p < 0.001) and a lower brittle-locator ratio than the comparison baseline suites.

The outputs of this research include a TathyaTest prototype at TRL 4 and a manuscript submitted for the Jurnal Teknologi Informasi dan Ilmu Komputer (JUTI). This research contributes to Software Testing and Quality Assurance through an automated test case generation method based on rendered-DOM crawling, forming the foundation of a five-year roadmap for TathyaTest's development with AI and machine learning integration.

